<div class="lp-hero"><div><p class="lp-kicker">The CallTeam buying desk / Calling methods</p><h1>Auto dialer vs <span>predictive dialer.</span><small>Power, parallel and the right choice for your team.</small></h1><p class="lp-intro">Choose a dialing method that fits your team, list and budget. Compare how each one works and where it falls short.</p><div class="lp-actions"><a class="lp-button" href="#comparison">Compare the dialing methods ↓</a><a class="lp-text-link" href="#choose-your-mode">Find your starting point →</a></div><p class="sg-brands">Close · Apollo · Nooks · Orum · Aircall · JustCall · CloudTalk</p></div><aside class="lp-brief"><p class="lp-kicker">CallTeam's starting point</p><h2>Can your team handle<br>the next answer?</h2><ol><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Account needs research?</strong><p>Keep time to read the record before calling.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Mostly waiting for answers?</strong><p>Test more lines against useful conversations.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Several callers available?</strong><p>Assess predictive pacing with the actual team.</p></div></li></ol><a href="#session-brief">Copy the session brief →</a></aside></div>
<p class="lp-direct-answer"><strong>The short answer:</strong> an auto dialer automates calling from a list. A predictive dialer adds pacing based on expected answers and available callers. For a small B2B team, we would start with single-line power, keep researched accounts and callbacks under direct control, and test parallel when waiting for answers is the real bottleneck.</p>
