<section class="lp-section" id="call-quality"><div class="lp-wrap"><div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">05 / Protect the conversation</p><h2>What happens when<br>somebody answers?</h2></div><div class="sg-two"><div><h3>Test the first few seconds.</h3><p>Answer detection can delay the caller joining. Use numbers you control to test a single answer, then two simultaneous answers. Listen from the prospect's side.</p><p>A voicemail, an AI screening assistant and the intended buyer are different outcomes. The caller needs a sensible next step for each one.</p></div><div><h3>Handle callbacks and stop requests.</h3><p>Call the displayed number back. Confirm where it rings, who owns the reply and whether the CRM keeps the history. Check that a stop request removes the person from every active calling queue.</p><p>Calling and recording requirements depend on the destination and setup. Use the <a href="/articles/b2b-cold-calling-compliance-global/">market-specific calling checks</a> before running the campaign.</p></div></div>
<div class="sg-note"><strong>AI dialer or AI voice agent?</strong> Answer detection, notes and coaching support a human caller. A voice agent speaks to the prospect itself. Confirm who speaks to the prospect before comparing prices.</div>
<div class="gr-resources"><h3>Have a useful opening ready.</h3><p>The dialer gets the call started. Your caller still needs a reason for the buyer to stay on the line.</p>{% include "components/free-calling-resources.njk" %}</div>
